
Neovim Dotfiles 🚀

A modular Neovim configuration written in Lua, focused on fast navigation, modern autocompletion, and a smooth Git workflow.


``
~/.config/nvim/
├── init.lua                 # Entry point: loads config + plugins
└── lua/
    ├── config/
    │   ├── options.lua      # Editor settings (numbers, tabs, search, etc.)
    │   └── keymaps.lua      # Global keybindings
    └── plugins/
        ├── fugitive.lua     # Git integration
        ├── lspconfig.lua    # Language Server Protocol (autocomplete, diagnostics, etc.)
        ├── lualine.lua      # Statusline
        ├── neo-tree.lua     # File explorer sidebar
        ├── oil.lua          # Edit the filesystem like a normal buffer
        ├── telescope.lua    # Fuzzy finder
        └── treesitter.lua   # Syntax highlighting and code parsing
`

🔌 Plugins & Their Key Functions

fugitive.lua — Git Integration
Run Git commands directly inside Neovim.

| Shortcut    | Function                          |
| :---------- | :-------------------------------- | 
| :Git        | Git status window                 |
| :Git blame  | Inline blame for the current file |
| :Git commit | Commit changes                    |
| :Git diff   | Show changes                      |
| :Git log    | Browse commit history             |
| :Git push   | Push to remote                    |
| :Git pull   | Pull to remote                    |
| <leader>gd  | Show diff for current file        |
| <leader>gb  | Toggle blame line                 |

\*Depending on your keymaps, add convenience bindings in keymaps.lua.

lspconfig.lua — Language Server & Autocompletion
Provides autocompletion, diagnostics, go-to-definition, references, hover docs, and refactoring.

| Shortcut | Function |
| :---     | :--- |
| gd       | Go to definition |
| gD       | Go to declaration |
| gi | Go to implementation |
| gr | List references |
| K | Hover documentation |
| [d / ]d | Previous / next diagnostic |
| <leader>ca | Code action |
| <leader>rn | Rename symbol |
| <leader>f | Format buffer |
| CTRL-SPACE | Trigger completion |
| CR | Accept completion |

Install servers with :Mason (if using mason.nvim).

lualine.lua — Statusline
A fast, customizable statusline written in Lua.

Highlights by default:
• Left: mode, Git branch, filename, diagnostics count
• Right: filetype, encoding, cursor position, line/col

Configure theme + sections in lualine.lua:
`lua
require('lualine').setup {
  options = { theme = 'gruvbox', sectionseparators = '', componentseparators = '' }
}
`

neo-tree.lua — File Explorer
A clean, modern sidebar file explorer.

| Shortcut | Function |
| :--- | :--- |
| <leader>e | Toggle file explorer |
| a | Add file |
| d | Delete file |
| r | Rename file |
| Enter | Open file |
| s | Open in split |
| v | Open in vsplit |
| / | Fuzzy filter |
| H / L | Toggle hidden files / last-opened |

oil.lua — Filesystem in a Buffer
Edit your filesystem like a normal buffer — rename files, move things around, all through text editing.

| Shortcut | Function |
| :--- | :--- |
| - | Open parent directory |
| Enter | Open file/directory under cursor |
| - (in oil buffer) | Go up a directory |
| Edit a filename | Rename file on save |
| g. | Toggle hidden files |
| g? | Show help |

oil.lua pairs nicely with neo-tree.lua — use oil for quick renames and neo-tree for browsing.

telescope.lua — Fuzzy Finder
Search files, buffers, Git history, LSP symbols, and more — with live preview.

| Shortcut | Function |
| :--- | :--- |
| <leader>ff | Find files |
| <leader>fg | Live grep (search inside files) |
| <leader>fb | Find open buffers |
| <leader>fh | Help tags |
| <leader>fr | Recent files |
| <leader>fs | Document symbols |
| <leader>fd | Diagnostics |
| <leader>gc | Git commits |

Inside Telescope: CTRL-n/CTRL-p to navigate, CTRL-t open in tab, CTRL-v open in vsplit.

treesitter.lua — Syntax Highlighting & Parsing
Provides accurate syntax highlighting, indentation, and code folding based on real parsers.

Features enabled:
• Incremental parsing for faster editing
• Syntax highlighting with nvim-treesitter
• Automatic indentation
• Textobjects for selecting functions, blocks, etc.

Install parsers with:
`vim
:TSInstall lua python javascript typescript go rust
`

| Shortcut | Function |
| :--- | :--- |
| :TSUpdate | Update all parsers |
| :TSInstall <lang> | Install a parser |
| af / if | Select a function / inner function |
| ac / ic | Select a class / inner class |
| aa / ia | Select a parameter / inner parameter |

⌨️ Global Keymaps (from keymaps.lua)

| Shortcut | Function |
| :--- | :--- |
| <leader>w | Save file |
| <leader>q | Quit |
| <leader>h | Clear search highlight |
| <C-h/j/k/l> | Move between splits |
| <leader>sv | Split vertically |
| <leader>sh | Split horizontally |
| <leader>tn | New tab |
| <leader>tc | Close tab |
| jk | Exit Insert mode |

> Replace <leader> (usually Space) with your preferred key in init.lua or options.lua.

🔧 Options Highlights (from options.lua)

Common settings you'll find:
• number = true — line numbers
• relativenumber = true — relative line numbers
• expandtab = true — spaces instead of tabs
• tabstop = 2 — two-space indentation
• shiftwidth = 2
• smartindent = true
• ignorecase = true + smartcase = true — smart case-insensitive search
• termguicolors = true — true-color support
• clipboard = "unnamedplus" — system clipboard integration
• undofile = true — persistent undo

🚀 Getting Started
Backup your existing config (just in case):
   `bash
   mv ~/.config/nvim ~/.config/nvim.bak
   `

Clone this repository:
   `bash
   git clone <your-repo-url> ~/.config/nvim
   `

Launch Neovim — plugins will be installed automatically on first startup.

Install language servers (via Mason or your package manager).

Install Treesitter parsers you need:
   `vim
   :TSInstall <language>
   `

📝 Notes
• Plugin manager: whichever is declared in init.lua (e.g. lazy.nvim / packer.nvim). Make sure to run :Lazy sync (or your manager's update command) after changing init.lua.
• If a keymap conflicts with a plugin, check keymaps.lua and the plugin's own config — the plugin's local mappings generally take precedence inside its buffer.
• Leader key is typically Space; adjust according to preference.

